    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented customerCode de-duplication in `ClinicServiceImpl.generateCustomerCode()` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`).\n\nThe method already computed a base code of the form `<REGION>-<HASH8>`. I added a collision check: it now gathers all existing owners' non-null `customerCode` values and, if the computed base already exists, appends `-<n>` with the smallest `n` \u2265 2 that produces a unique code (e.g. `NSW-1A2B3C4D-2`, then `-3`, etc.). When there's no collision the base code is returned unchanged.\n\nThe lookup reuses the existing `ownerRepository.findAll().stream()` idiom already used by `countNamesakes` and `countOwnersInCity` in the same class, and all required imports (`Set`, `Objects`, `Collectors`) were already present.\n\nTests: `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (the `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` case asserting distinct owners always get distinct customerCodes).",
