    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change fits this file's established conventions cleanly:\n\n- **Right unit / cohesion.** De-duplication lives inside `generateCustomerCode`, whose job is to produce the stored `customerCode`. Uniqueness of that code is part of generating it, so the logic belongs here rather than being hoisted into `saveOwner` or a separate collaborator. The method reads as a single responsibility (\"generate a unique customer code\") and stays short (~18 lines).\n\n- **Idiomatic.** Scanning `ownerRepository.findAll().stream()` to derive a value is the dominant pattern in this class (`countNamesakes`, `countOwnersInCity`, `countRegisteredToday`, `findPossibleDuplicateOf`, `isHouseholdInUse`, `decorateWithHouseholdMemberCount` all do exactly this). The `.map(...).filter(Objects::nonNull).collect(Collectors.toSet())` style matches surrounding code, and the required imports (`Set`, `Objects`, `Collectors`) were already present.\n\n- **No duplication / no catch-all.** Nothing else in the class performs code de-duplication, so no existing helper is being reinvented, and the method isn't accreting unrelated concerns.\n\n- **Docs.** The Javadoc was updated to describe the new collision behavior with a concrete example, consistent with the detailed doc style used throughout the file.\n\nA maintainer of this codebase would find the addition natural.",
